  "notes": {
    "content": [
      "The page continues a definition: the infimum in the family F is the empty figure, its least element, and disjoint figures are compatible.",
      "It states (1.13) after “On a, par les axiomes:”. The right member combines an empty intersection of ombres and elementwise compatibility. The explanatory paragraph restates this using the absence of common lieux and disjointness between lieux of the two figures.",
      "It stresses compatibility and disjunction on the subcollections M and L. In the set-theoretic case, it calls these relations trivial on L: two lieux are always compatible and are disjoint iff distinct. The last sentence begins a contrast even in the set-theoretic moderate case and is unfinished at the page foot."
    ],
    "math_reading_decisions": [
      "Literal om(G), without b, is retained in both lower occurrences of (1.13); it is not normalized to the expected omb spelling.",
      "The displayed condition says compatible; the later prose says disjoint after corrections. Neither is silently rewritten to the other.",
      "The long crossbar of tout is distinguished from a deletion; the barred m at the foot is a verbal abbreviation, not an equality sign.",
      "S’s proposed axiom refinement is separated from the page’s literal attribution. No other-page axiom, countermodel or proof has been consulted or verified."
    ],
